            <ArticleTitle>Chelating P2-Bis-phosphazenes with a (R,R)-1,2-Diaminocyclohexane Skeleton: Two New Chiral Superbases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2591-2598</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/chem.201604522</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The linkage of two P2 -phosphazenyl groups through a C2 -symmetric (R,R)-1,2-diaminocyclohexane (DACH) backbone yielded the new chiral superbases DACH-P2 NMe2 and DACH-P2 Pyr (Pyr=pyrrolidinyl). These bases were prepared by a Kirsanov reaction and studied with respect to their spectroscopic and structural characteristics. Theoretical calculations concerning their basicity properties revealed remarkable pKBH+ values of 38.1 and 39.9 on the acetonitrile scale; this makes them the strongest nonionic chiral superbases known to date.</AbstractText>
